    "description": "In this video, Nicole shows you how to make homemade pepper jelly. This southern staple recipe uses diced bell peppers and jalapeños to make a sweet and tangy jelly spread. After stirring and boiling the peppers in a sauce pan with apple cider vinegar, fruit pectin, and sugar, add the mixture to sterilized glass containers. Once the jars have been sealed, let them sit in the simmering water to finish the process. Whether it’s spread on a cracker or a burger, this multi-purpose jelly should be in every kitchen.",
